      The main drawback is efficiency: updating all ancestors for every file makes parsing cost O(F * H) where H is directory depth. For AoC Day 7, H is usually small enough, but the plan’s worst-case complexity could be significantly worse than the tree/DFS approaches. It also includes an edge-case note about `must_free <= 0` outputting 0 or smallest directory size—this is ambiguous relative to the puzzle’s “delete a directory” interpretation, though it says “handle it safely.”
      
      Overall: correctness is strong, but feasibility/efficiency is weaker than Plans 1 and 2.
    
